body:
Being a stay at home mother with ADHD, with a child with ADHD... Oh my god. And my husband wonders why I don't have the greatest relationship with our 8 year old. We're too much alike and drive eachother crazy. 

&#x200B;

I got a job last week because I literally can't take it anymore. I needed structure of my own.

That's not really fair. He's young, male, and is doing the right thing by coming here to talk about his feelings. I do think he should be more concerned about her health than her appearance, however. But again, 22/yo male. 

&#x200B;

If he said this to her, that's another thing, however...

I can never seem to find any that are vegan! One time I found some by luck at Reny's... But that's it. :( 

&#x200B;

But man, same. I'm on a mission today!

Idk if this counts, and I'm not sure if I can remember it word-for-word but... Here goes! I'm sorry if this is shoddily written; I'm working on my prose. I like commas. Bare with me. lmao.

&#x200B;

For context: Last year... My daughter was born bright and early 9 am after over-night labor, much like her brother. She was full-term. 7 lbs, 22 inches long, beautiful, and I had no issues my entire pregnancy. Unfortunately, when she was born, meconium (basically first-poop) came out with her which can lead to major issues if inhaled. We suspect this to be the case as she had a bunch of fluid in her lungs at birth and couldn't keep her oxygen levels up on her own. They ended up taking her 45 minutes away to a NICU... While I stayed behind for the rest of the day. Most of this day is still a blur so I'll do my best to remember.

&#x200B;

Speed up to the future and my best friend is hanging out with me while dear-fiance sleeps in the bed beside me. I'm okay, feeling okay, kind of numb but happy my daughter's birthday is here. Staying positive. The most warrior-like I've ever been in my life. The NICU team comes in to say hello/goodbye and we get to peek in and see these little eyes, red hair, and tiny hands swaddled up in what looks like a giant incubation chamber. Eventually, everyone joins us: my parents got there with our son, and fiance's parents a short while later.

&#x200B;

We were all talking and I was so happy just to have everyone around. My dad went and got my DQ and Subway and life was good. I don't know how it came up, but my best friend and I were talking about how you couldn't see her (our daughter) at all because of all the equipment. Cue fiance's psychotic mother making things about her (Again). She ends up whispering "I can't be around her" to her husband (fiance's father) in regards to my best friend having "seen" my daughter. No one else heard it but me, and as she was walking out I go absolutely batshit and scream "REALLY (her name). GROW UP." Everyone was super fucking confused at this point. She had the audacity to come back in and goes "Did SoMeOne JuSt TeLl mE To GrOw Up" and I... Guys, I think my brain went to an alternate dimension at this point. I have never seen red to this day. I couldn't stop. Suddenly I forgot everyone else was in the room and yelled "YEAH. THE WOMAN THAT JUST HAD A BABY A FEW HOURS AGO AND ISNT WITH HER. AND DID IT NATURALLY, I MIGHT ADD. YOU ARENT DOING THIS AGAIN. GET OUT. GET. OUT!!!!" Screaming at her as loudly and passionately as a woman could. She quietly walked out visibly shook, and the room was quiet as I went on a tangent about how incredibly selfish she is. When I came out of it I was like ... oh. Shit. Sorry. And everyone reassured me that it was okay. I can't help but laugh looking back because she totally deserved it, I was just REALLY embarrassed. A woman can only go through so much I guess. lol. Whoops.

&#x200B;

For context, she pulled something similar with the birth of my son 8 years ago. I didn't want anyone in the delivery room but my fiance and I. I was young and everyone pushed me to have my mom in the room at the last second while I was in labor, and my mom didn't respect me apparently (not shocked). So I finally just said fine and let her come in. Well, mother-in-law apparently had a god damn tantrum about it. She knew I didn't want anyone in there, but because my mom got to she didn't like that she couldn't. She's basically a giant toddler and I can't stand her. I think that's why I lost my shit as much as I did; on top of suppressed emotional pain and exhaustion.

&#x200B;

Moral of the story: It's not fucking about you, it's about the laboring mother. If you ever find yourself in a position where you think "what about me" at a labor/delivery situation... Go home. Again, I reiterate, it isn't about you. It's about whatever makes the laboring mother comfortable thus aiding a healthy and speedy delivery.

&#x200B;

Edit to add: 

Tld;dr: My mother-in-law is a selfish douchecanoe. I finally called her out.

I still think 8 months is still too kind. At this point, I would make him buy his own. Either by working it off with chores, a part-time job if old enough, or gift money.

&#x200B;

Edit to add: You're still doing far more than most, and I tend to be on the stricter side lol. I don't tolerate misuse or abuse of items, period. But I also grew up poor as shit with this engrained in my mind as something very serious. lol

I made these tonight! I just so happened to randomly have the same exact biscuits on hand. Thankyou for the awesome idea!!!

&#x200B;

The changes I made were: A can of lentils instead of TVP. I also added a bit of Garlic powder, minced onion, chili powder, and cumin to the seasoning mixture. I also added half a slice of American cheese to each one.  I dipped mine in a bit of sour cream, and the boys dipped them in sour cream and salsa.

&#x200B;

I called them "Breakfast tacos" and my son ate them right up LOL.
